  "note": "Election of the Newry Urban Council, polled Wednesday 18 May 1955 (Belfast News-Letter, 20 May 1955, p. 8). The six North Ward seats were filled without a poll (Newry Telegraph, 7 May 1955, p. 7). The paper heads the list 'Six Unionists returned unopposed'; no label is printed against the names. Joseph McCullough and John F. Bradfield were new members; Brian Ingram and Robert McGrann did not seek re-election. Returned unopposed."
